Clarity does not bundle third-party weights, ffmpeg, x264, x265, or GPL code.
Weights are downloaded at runtime into the shared Voxprint models folder after
a SHA-256 check. Only MIT, Apache-2.0, and BSD weights are accepted.

Third-party code and models
---------------------------

KAIR (Kai Zhang, 2019) — MIT License
  DRUNet colour and DRUNet deblocking colour weights
  https://github.com/cszn/KAIR
  DPIR, which defines the DRUNet deblocking input, is also MIT.
  https://github.com/cszn/DPIR

SCUNet (Kai Zhang) — Apache License 2.0
  The SCUNet repository is Apache-2.0. The colour real_psnr weight used here
  is hosted on the KAIR v1.0 release (MIT).
  https://github.com/cszn/SCUNet

Real-ESRGAN (Xintao Wang, 2021) — BSD 3-Clause License
  realesr-general-x4v3, its wdn counterpart, and realesr-animevideov3.
  https://github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN

PyTorch — BSD-style licence. Clarity pins torch 2.14.1 with CUDA 13.0 wheels.
  https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch

ONNX Runtime — MIT License, used through the shared voxprint-engine package
  from Voxprint AI Enlarge. Clarity does not vendor that package.

PySide6 / Qt — GNU LGPL. Linked as a dependency, not vendored.

NumPy — BSD 3-Clause License.
Pillow — MIT-style Historical Permission Notice and Disclaimer, plus the
  Pillow licence.

ffmpeg — GNU LGPL build, installed separately. Clarity does not ship ffmpeg,
  x264, or x265. H.264 output is refused. H.265 is hevc_nvenc only.

Elephants Dream — Creative Commons Attribution. Used only as the benchmark
  clip (Blender Foundation / Netherlands Media Art Institute). It is not
  bundled in this repository.
